# Config for .codex/cron/run-daily-debt.sh — the daily unattended Codex
# tech-debt runner.
#
# Copy this file to debt-runner.env (same directory) and fill it in. The
# real file is gitignored — it holds a live repo URL and paths, and may end
# up holding secrets, so it never gets committed.
#
#   cp .codex/cron/debt-runner.env.example .codex/cron/debt-runner.env

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------

# Git remote to clone/push. HTTPS is simplest if `gh` is already
# authenticated on this machine (the script pushes with plain `git push`,
# which uses gh's stored git credential helper over HTTPS).
REPO_URL=https://github.com/peterdrier/Humans.git

# No API key here. This runner uses Codex plan quota via a ChatGPT sign-in,
# so the credential lives where `codex login` puts it (~/.codex by default,
# or $CODEX_HOME), owned by the user the timer runs as. The preflight checks
# that sign-in and fails fast if it has expired.
#
# Set CODEX_HOME only if the credential is not in the default location.
#CODEX_HOME=/home/peter/.codex

# --- Usually fine as-is -------------------------------------------------

# Dedicated clone directory. NEVER point this at a human's working checkout
# — the script hard-resets and cleans it on every run. Defaults to a path
# under $HOME so it works for whichever user the timer runs as.
# WORK_DIR=$HOME/.humans-debt-runner/clone

# Where logs land. Must stay outside WORK_DIR (git clean would delete it).
# LOG_DIR=$HOME/.humans-debt-runner/logs

# Wall-clock budget for the codex run itself (anything `timeout` accepts,
# e.g. 90m, 2h). The wrapper sends SIGINT at the cap, then SIGKILL 120s
# later if codex hasn't exited.
# TIME_BUDGET=90m

# Model + reasoning effort, pinned explicitly rather than inherited from
# codex's interactive config — otherwise changing Peter's own day-to-day
# preference silently changes what the nightly job runs too.
# CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# CODEX_EFFORT=medium

# Branch created each run is ${BRANCH_PREFIX}/YYYY-MM-DD.
# BRANCH_PREFIX=codex/daily-debt

# Base branch on origin the run branches from and PRs target.
# GH_BASE_BRANCH=main

# 1 = codex runs with --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox (needed in
# environments where codex's own sandbox, e.g. bwrap, fails — see
# .codex/README.md's "Why It Works This Way"). 0 = --full-auto instead.
# CODEX_DANGEROUS=1

# Push retries (network failures only), exponential backoff starting at 2s.
# PUSH_RETRIES=4

# How many days of debt-YYYY-MM-DD.log files to keep in LOG_DIR.
# LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# --- Usually not needed --------------------------------------------------

# GH_TOKEN: only set this if `gh` is NOT already logged in on this machine,
# or you want to override the logged-in account for this runner. The script
# preflights with `gh auth status` and fails loudly if that doesn't pass —
# on a machine where `gh auth login` has already been run interactively,
# leave this unset and gh's own stored credentials are used.
# GH_TOKEN=
